{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9vExNwBUqRiUZcA8xX1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--and` patterns now get the same path-separator error as the main pattern. Before, `fd foo --and dir/x` quietly returned nothing; now it fails with the \"contains a path-separation character\" message naming `dir/x`. The full test suite passes. The change isn't committed: git has no author name or email set here, and I didn't want to set one for you. It's sitting on a new branch, `fix-and-pattern-path-separator`.\n\n- **`src/main.rs`:** `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs its existing check on the main pattern and then on each `--and` pattern, stopping at the first one with a separator. Most of the diff is re-indentation. `--full-path` still skips the check for all of them, and the Windows-only `\\` handling is unchanged.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** new test `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`.\n- **`CHANGELOG.md`:** one entry under Unreleased → Bugfixes.\n\n**Testing:**\n- The new test failed before the fix for the expected reason (no error was printed). I also put the old `src/main.rs` back temporarily and confirmed the test fails again.\n- `cargo test -q`: 139 unit and 111 integration tests pass.\n- `cargo fmt --check` passes.\n- `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` on the source code passes.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets` reports errors in `tests/tests.rs` (for example line 2539). They were already there before my change: the unchanged tree shows 18 errors and mine shows 15, so I left them alone.\n\nThe Windows `\\` path didn't run, because this machine is Linux. That part of the logic is identical; it now just runs once per pattern.\n\nTo commit: `git commit -am \"fix: flag path separators in --and patterns\"` once your git name and email are configured."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":44470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":436,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ba9fc17-122f-4dfc-8af1-4914a4b5a5e8","uuid":"6a983d6f-63aa-4694-9693-cc5fb54e4ece","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:12:56.255Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9vExBGYLVWXfe1fkZWJ"}
